{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "x^2 + 1 = (x + 2) (x + 3) over GF(5)\n  how: square-free split (gcd(f, f'), p-th roots where f' = 0), distinct-degree split (gcd(x^(q^i) - x, f)), Cantor-Zassenhaus equal-degree split\n  check: the product of the factors is f; each factor is irreducible (Rabin); Berlekamp counts 2 distinct factors\n  roots in GF(5): 2 by evaluation at every element, the number of distinct linear factors (2)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "ring_factor", "ucas": "factor x^2+1 over GF(5)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "factor", "method": "square-free split (gcd(f, f'), p-th roots where f' = 0), distinct-degree split (gcd(x^(q^i) - x, f)), Cantor-Zassenhaus equal-degree split", "roots_in_gf_5": "2 by evaluation at every element, the number of distinct linear factors (2)", "lhs": "x^2 + 1", "over": "GF(5)", "value": "(x + 2) (x + 3)", "headline": "x^2 + 1 = (x + 2) (x + 3) over GF(5)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the product of the factors is f; each factor is irreducible (Rabin); Berlekamp counts 2 distinct factors"}], "files": [], "text": "x^2 + 1 = (x + 2) (x + 3) over GF(5)\n  how: square-free split (gcd(f, f'), p-th roots where f' = 0), distinct-degree split (gcd(x^(q^i) - x, f)), Cantor-Zassenhaus equal-degree split\n  check: the product of the factors is f; each factor is irreducible (Rabin); Berlekamp counts 2 distinct factors\n  roots in GF(5): 2 by evaluation at every element, the number of distinct linear factors (2)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "x^3 + x + 1 is irreducible over GF(2)\n  how: square-free split (gcd(f, f'), p-th roots where f' = 0), distinct-degree split (gcd(x^(q^i) - x, f)), Cantor-Zassenhaus equal-degree split (by the trace map)\n  check: the product of the factors is f; each factor is irreducible (Rabin); Berlekamp counts 1 distinct factor\n  roots in GF(2): 0 by evaluation at every element, the number of distinct linear factors (0)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "ring_factor", "ucas": "factor x^3+x+1 over GF(2)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "factor", "method": "square-free split (gcd(f, f'), p-th roots where f' = 0), distinct-degree split (gcd(x^(q^i) - x, f)), Cantor-Zassenhaus equal-degree split (by the trace map)", "roots_in_gf_2": "0 by evaluation at every element, the number of distinct linear factors (0)", "headline": "x^3 + x + 1 is irreducible over GF(2)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the product of the factors is f; each factor is irreducible (Rabin); Berlekamp counts 1 distinct factor"}], "files": [], "text": "x^3 + x + 1 is irreducible over GF(2)\n  how: square-free split (gcd(f, f'), p-th roots where f' = 0), distinct-degree split (gcd(x^(q^i) - x, f)), Cantor-Zassenhaus equal-degree split (by the trace map)\n  check: the product of the factors is f; each factor is irreducible (Rabin); Berlekamp counts 1 distinct factor\n  roots in GF(2): 0 by evaluation at every element, the number of distinct linear factors (0)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "x^4 + x^3 + x^2 + x + 1 is irreducible over GF(2)\n  how: square-free split (gcd(f, f'), p-th roots where f' = 0), distinct-degree split (gcd(x^(q^i) - x, f)), Cantor-Zassenhaus equal-degree split (by the trace map)\n  check: the product of the factors is f; each factor is irreducible (Rabin); Berlekamp counts 1 distinct factor\n  roots in GF(2): 0 by evaluation at every element, the number of distinct linear factors (0)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 3, "ok": true, "cmd": "ring_factor", "ucas": "factor x^4+x^3+x^2+x+1 over GF(2)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "factor", "method": "square-free split (gcd(f, f'), p-th roots where f' = 0), distinct-degree split (gcd(x^(q^i) - x, f)), Cantor-Zassenhaus equal-degree split (by the trace map)", "roots_in_gf_2": "0 by evaluation at every element, the number of distinct linear factors (0)", "headline": "x^4 + x^3 + x^2 + x + 1 is irreducible over GF(2)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the product of the factors is f; each factor is irreducible (Rabin); Berlekamp counts 1 distinct factor"}], "files": [], "text": "x^4 + x^3 + x^2 + x + 1 is irreducible over GF(2)\n  how: square-free split (gcd(f, f'), p-th roots where f' = 0), distinct-degree split (gcd(x^(q^i) - x, f)), Cantor-Zassenhaus equal-degree split (by the trace map)\n  check: the product of the factors is f; each factor is irreducible (Rabin); Berlekamp counts 1 distinct factor\n  roots in GF(2): 0 by evaluation at every element, the number of distinct linear factors (0)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "x^2 + 1 is irreducible over GF(3)\n  how: Rabin's test (degree 2: x^(q^2) = x mod f, and gcd(x^(q^(2/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 2; q = 3)\n  check: Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp: 1 distinct irreducible factor; trial division by every monic polynomial of degree <= 1: none divides\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 4, "ok": true, "cmd": "irreducible", "ucas": "irreducible x^2+1 over GF(3)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "irreducible", "method": "Rabin's test (degree 2: x^(q^2) = x mod f, and gcd(x^(q^(2/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 2; q = 3)", "headline": "x^2 + 1 is irreducible over GF(3)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp: 1 distinct irreducible factor; trial division by every monic polynomial of degree <= 1: none divides"}], "files": [], "text": "x^2 + 1 is irreducible over GF(3)\n  how: Rabin's test (degree 2: x^(q^2) = x mod f, and gcd(x^(q^(2/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 2; q = 3)\n  check: Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp: 1 distinct irreducible factor; trial division by every monic polynomial of degree <= 1: none divides\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 5, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "x^2 + 1 is not irreducible over GF(5)\n  how: Rabin's test (degree 2: x^(q^2) = x mod f, and gcd(x^(q^(2/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 2; q = 5)\n  x^2 + 1 = (x + 2) (x + 3)\n  check: Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp: 2 distinct irreducible factors; trial division by every monic polynomial of degree <= 1: a factor found\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 5, "ok": true, "cmd": "irreducible", "ucas": "irreducible x^2+1 over GF(5)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "irreducible", "method": "Rabin's test (degree 2: x^(q^2) = x mod f, and gcd(x^(q^(2/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 2; q = 5)", "headline": "x^2 + 1 is not irreducible over GF(5)", "details": ["x^2 + 1 = (x + 2) (x + 3)"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp: 2 distinct irreducible factors; trial division by every monic polynomial of degree <= 1: a factor found"}], "files": [], "text": "x^2 + 1 is not irreducible over GF(5)\n  how: Rabin's test (degree 2: x^(q^2) = x mod f, and gcd(x^(q^(2/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 2; q = 5)\n  x^2 + 1 = (x + 2) (x + 3)\n  check: Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp: 2 distinct irreducible factors; trial division by every monic polynomial of degree <= 1: a factor found\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 6, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "x^3 + x + 1 is irreducible over GF(2)\n  how: Rabin's test (degree 3: x^(q^3) = x mod f, and gcd(x^(q^(3/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 3; q = 2)\n  check: Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp: 1 distinct irreducible factor; trial division by every monic polynomial of degree <= 1: none divides\nprimitive: x has order 7 = q^3 - 1 = 7\n  how: x^((q^n - 1)/r) != 1 mod f for each prime r | q^n - 1 = 7\n  so an LFSR with this feedback polynomial has period 7 (maximal: every nonzero state)\n  check: stepping x, x^2, ... mod f: x^k = 1 first at k = 7\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 6, "ok": true, "cmd": "primitive", "ucas": "primitive x^3+x+1 over GF(2)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "primitive", "method": ["Rabin's test (degree 3: x^(q^3) = x mod f, and gcd(x^(q^(3/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 3; q = 2)", "x^((q^n - 1)/r) != 1 mod f for each prime r | q^n - 1 = 7"], "headline": "x^3 + x + 1 is irreducible over GF(2)", "more": ["primitive: x has order 7 = q^3 - 1 = 7"], "details": ["so an LFSR with this feedback polynomial has period 7 (maximal: every nonzero state)"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp: 1 distinct irreducible factor; trial division by every monic polynomial of degree <= 1: none divides"}, {"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "stepping x, x^2, ... mod f: x^k = 1 first at k = 7"}], "files": [], "text": "x^3 + x + 1 is irreducible over GF(2)\n  how: Rabin's test (degree 3: x^(q^3) = x mod f, and gcd(x^(q^(3/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 3; q = 2)\n  check: Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp: 1 distinct irreducible factor; trial division by every monic polynomial of degree <= 1: none divides\nprimitive: x has order 7 = q^3 - 1 = 7\n  how: x^((q^n - 1)/r) != 1 mod f for each prime r | q^n - 1 = 7\n  so an LFSR with this feedback polynomial has period 7 (maximal: every nonzero state)\n  check: stepping x, x^2, ... mod f: x^k = 1 first at k = 7\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 7, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "x^4 + x^3 + x^2 + x + 1 is irreducible over GF(2)\n  how: Rabin's test (degree 4: x^(q^4) = x mod f, and gcd(x^(q^(4/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 4; q = 2)\n  check: Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp: 1 distinct irreducible factor; trial division by every monic polynomial of degree <= 2: none divides\nnot primitive: x has order 5 < q^4 - 1 = 15\n  how: x^((q^n - 1)/r) != 1 mod f for each prime r | q^n - 1 = 3 * 5\n  so an LFSR with this feedback polynomial has period 5\n  check: stepping x, x^2, ... mod f: x^k = 1 first at k = 5\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 7, "ok": true, "cmd": "primitive", "ucas": "primitive x^4+x^3+x^2+x+1 over GF(2)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "primitive", "method": ["Rabin's test (degree 4: x^(q^4) = x mod f, and gcd(x^(q^(4/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 4; q = 2)", "x^((q^n - 1)/r) != 1 mod f for each prime r | q^n - 1 = 3 * 5"], "headline": "x^4 + x^3 + x^2 + x + 1 is irreducible over GF(2)", "more": ["not primitive: x has order 5 < q^4 - 1 = 15"], "details": ["so an LFSR with this feedback polynomial has period 5"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp: 1 distinct irreducible factor; trial division by every monic polynomial of degree <= 2: none divides"}, {"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "stepping x, x^2, ... mod f: x^k = 1 first at k = 5"}], "files": [], "text": "x^4 + x^3 + x^2 + x + 1 is irreducible over GF(2)\n  how: Rabin's test (degree 4: x^(q^4) = x mod f, and gcd(x^(q^(4/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 4; q = 2)\n  check: Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp: 1 distinct irreducible factor; trial division by every monic polynomial of degree <= 2: none divides\nnot primitive: x has order 5 < q^4 - 1 = 15\n  how: x^((q^n - 1)/r) != 1 mod f for each prime r | q^n - 1 = 3 * 5\n  so an LFSR with this feedback polynomial has period 5\n  check: stepping x, x^2, ... mod f: x^k = 1 first at k = 5\n"}, "isError": false}}
